+# Todo Due Date Implementation Plan
+
+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [x]`) syntax for tracking.
+
+**Goal:** Add optional due dates, strict validation, and overdue filtering to the API and list for ticket #1.
+
+**Architecture:** Store validated dates as nullable `DateOnly`. Request DTOs accept strings;
+PATCH tracks whether `dueDate` was supplied. A shared overdue predicate uses a UTC calendar date
+from `TimeProvider`. The Blazor page reads the store directly and filters with a checkbox.
+
+**Tech Stack:** Existing .NET 10, Blazor interactive server, xUnit, WebApplicationFactory, Playwright MCP.
+
+**Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-15-todo-due-date-design.md`
+
+## Global Constraints
+
+- No new NuGet packages.
+- Store validation throws `System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations.ValidationException`.
+- Invalid API inputs return HTTP 400 with `{"error":"…"}`.
+- Every new UI element used by tests carries `data-testid`.
+- UI: display and checkbox only; use the store directly.
+- Overdue: open and date strictly before today's UTC calendar date.
+- API `dueDate`: `YYYY-MM-DD`; absent PATCH preserves, `null` clears.
+
+## Review Focus
+
+- An invalid PATCH must preserve the title, completion state and original due date.
+- Missing versus explicit null on PATCH must not be conflated.
+- Today and completed past-due items must never pass the overdue filter.
+- Leap days, unpadded dates, timestamp strings and non-string JSON inputs need coverage.
+- Time must be read when querying, so advancing UTC midnight changes overdue results.
+
+### Task 1: Due date API and store
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/TodoStore.cs`, `src/DemoTodo/Program.cs`,
+`tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoApiTests.cs`, `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoStoreTests.cs`;
+create `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/FixedTimeProvider.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:** Keep existing constructor calls valid. Add `DateOnly? DueDate = null` to `Todo`,
+optional `string? DueDate = null` to `NewTodo`, presence-tracked `DueDate` to `TodoPatch`.
+Produce `Todo.IsOverdue(DateOnly today)`, `TodoStore.Today`, `TodoStore.List(bool overdueOnly = false)`.
+Register `TimeProvider.System`; an optional store clock preserves direct construction.
+
+- [x] Write API tests for round trip, omitted/null dates, PATCH set/change/preserve/clear,
+  invalid create/update and unchanged stored data, leap days, JSON types, overdue boundaries.
+  Assert literal ISO dates and HTTP 400 JSON errors. Inject a fixed UTC clock via the test factory.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test`; expect assertion failures because dates are ignored and filtering is absent.
+- [x] Implement the DTOs, strict invariant date parsing and atomic updates in the store;
+  wire optional boolean query filtering and the clock in `Program.cs`.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test`; expect all API/store tests to pass.
+- [x] Commit: `feat: support optional due dates and overdue API filtering`.
+
+### Task 2: List display and interactive filter
+
+**Files:** Modify `src/DemoTodo/Components/Pages/Home.razor` and
+`tests/DemoTodo.Tests/TodoApiTests.cs`.
+
+**Interfaces:** Consume Task 1's store and overdue predicate. Add test IDs
+`overdue-filter`, `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`; retain existing IDs.
+
+- [x] Write a prerendered-page test seeded with past/today/future/completed/undated items;
+  expect a date next to titles, exactly one overdue label, and the checkbox label.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test`; expect the page test to fail on missing date markup.
+- [x] Render dates as semantic `time` elements in ISO format, the exact label „überfällig“,
+  and a bound checkbox „nur überfällige“ that filters directly through the store.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test`; expect the full suite to pass.
+- [x] Commit: `feat: display due dates and filter overdue todos in the list`.
+
+### Task 3: Review, browser verification and delivery
+
+**Files:** No additional product features; update this plan's completion checkboxes.
+
+- [x] Review the full branch with a fresh reviewer; address important findings via failing tests.
+- [x] Start the app as described in `AGENTS.md`, wait for `/health`, and use Playwright MCP
+  to verify date lifecycle, invalid dates, API filtering, display, and checkbox on/off/empty states.
+  Save screenshots outside the repository and stop the app.
+- [x] Run `dotnet test` and `git diff --check`, commit the final documentation state.
+- [x] Push the ticket branch, create a draft PR against `main`, post implementation/cost summaries,
+  and move ticket #1 to `status:review`. Do not merge, publish, or close the ticket.
